course: dictionary
lesson: 1613
title: Chemical: a word with two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A chemical can be a noun or an adjective, so the words around it show you which one it is. «A battery stores energy in chemicals and pushes electricity round the circuit.» Here chemicals is a noun, meaning the substances inside the battery that hold energy.
explain: Look at the word that follows. «A battery stores chemical energy and pushes electricity around a circuit.» Chemical comes before energy and describes it, so it is an adjective, meaning to do with chemistry or how substances change.
explain: Context also shows you what a word does, not only what it is. «Photos were developed with chemicals in a dark room.» The dark room and the developing are your clues. Swap in a meaning: «developed with substances» still makes sense, so you know you have it right.
fact: A chemical is a substance, such as salt, oxygen or bleach.
fact: As an adjective, «chemical» means to do with chemistry or how substances change, as in «a chemical reaction».
fact: A chemical reaction makes new substances, like burning, rusting or baking a cake.
fact: Everything around you is made of chemicals, including water and air.
fact: Household chemicals such as bleach and weedkiller are harmful: never mix them, never drink them, and keep them out of reach of little children.
exercise: «When the chemicals are used up, the push stops and the battery is flat.» What are the chemicals here? | The buttons you press to turn it on | Wires that carry electricity round the circuit | Dust that gathers on the battery | *Substances inside the battery that store energy
exercise: «A battery stores chemical energy.» In this sentence, chemical is a | question word | noun, meaning a cloud of gas | *adjective, describing the energy | verb, meaning to store
exercise: Which of these is a chemical reaction? | Reading a book in bed | Sitting quietly in the sun | Walking to school in the rain | *Baking a cake
test: «The aches all over in flu come mostly from the immune system's chemical messengers.» Chemical messengers means | Doctors who study germs | Messages written on paper | Pills you swallow with water | *Substances in the body that carry signals
test: Which household chemical is dangerous to drink? | Milk | *Bleach | Orange juice | Water
exam: In which sentence is chemical an adjective? | «Bleach is a dangerous chemical.» | «Oxygen is a chemical in the air.» | *«A chemical reaction makes new substances.» | «Store the chemicals out of reach.»
